# .cursorrules — Asset Pricing Characteristics Framework

## Project context

This repository builds a transparent, configurable framework for constructing
empirical asset pricing characteristics from WRDS data.

The primary goal is to reproduce GKX datashare.csv by identifying every
implementation convention used in its construction. The baseline is a validated
replication of Green's SAS implementation.

All investigation work follows the staged reconstruction process documented in
docs/agent/INVESTIGATION_PROTOCOL.md.

## What this project is NOT

This is not a project to produce matching numbers by any means necessary.
It is a project to understand exactly WHY different implementations differ.
Every discrepancy must be explained by a named, configurable parameter.

## Required reading before any code change

Before making any change related to characteristic construction or data pipeline,
read these files:

  docs/agent/AGENT_RULES.md
  docs/agent/CONVENTIONS_REGISTRY.yaml
  docs/agent/DISCREPANCY_TABLE.csv

## Core constraints for all code in this repo

1. The Green replication must remain reproducible at all times.
   Never break the Green baseline configuration.

2. Every implementation choice must be a configurable parameter.
   No hard-coded conventions inside construction functions.

3. Convention changes and formula changes must never be conflated.
   They are tracked in separate files for a reason.

4. Every test must report Spearman AND sample N AND unique permnos.
   Spearman alone is never sufficient to claim a match.

5. Hypotheses must be tested one at a time, across all affected
   characteristics, never stacked.

## File structure that must be respected

  src/                     — characteristic construction code
  src/config/              — ConventionConfig class and defaults
  src/pipeline/            — data pipeline (CRSP pull, CCM merge, etc.)
  src/characteristics/     — one file per characteristic or characteristic family
  docs/agent/              — agent rules, registry, table, log (DO NOT RESTRUCTURE)
  scripts/                 — validation and comparison scripts (NOT for public repo)
  supplementary/           — reference files (datashare.csv, Green output, etc.)

## ConventionConfig must be the single source of truth

All configurable conventions must be accessed through the ConventionConfig object.
No characteristic construction function may read configuration from anywhere else.

```python
# Correct
def build_ep(data: pd.DataFrame, config: ConventionConfig) -> pd.DataFrame:
    if config.industry_averaging_timing == 'post_crsp_merge':
        ...

# Wrong — hard-coded convention
def build_ep(data: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:
    # always uses post-merge — not reproducible for Green
    ...
```

## Validation script interface

Every characteristic must have a corresponding validation entry that can be run with:

  python scripts/validate_characteristic.py --char [name] --target [green|gkx]

This script must output all five required metrics:
  Spearman vs target, Sample N, GKX N, Unique permnos, GKX permnos

## What belongs in git and what does not

IN the repo:
  src/, docs/agent/, tests/, README.md, requirements.txt, .cursorrules

NOT in the repo:
  scripts/ (validation scripts), supplementary/ (data files), docs/validations/

## README principles

The README must clearly state:
  - This repository prioritizes reproducibility and transparency
  - Every implementation decision is a named, configurable parameter
  - The framework can reproduce multiple published datasets by changing config
  - Green's output is the validated baseline; GKX datashare.csv is the target
